course: dictionary
lesson: 2003
title: What is a concert?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A concert is a show where people play music or sing for an audience. The audience is the people who sit and watch and listen. Look at the words around the word to see what it means. «At a concert, play or assembly you stay quiet during the show and clap at the end.» Quiet, show and clap all tell you that a concert is an event where people listen and watch.
explain: The same word can have a second meaning. «In concert» means working together. «The orchestra tunes to one note, so everyone plays in tune together.» Here the players are acting as one group, so in concert means together.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Before a concert the orchestra tunes to one note, usually an A played by the oboe.» If you swap in show of music, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A concert is a show where people play music or sing for an audience.
fact: «In concert» also means working together, as a team.
fact: At a concert you usually stay quiet during the show and clap at the end.
fact: Before a concert, the orchestra tunes to one note, usually an A played by the oboe, so everyone plays in tune together.
fact: The kora of West Africa has 21 strings, and the Chinese erhu has 2 strings and is bowed.
exercise: «At a concert, play or assembly you stay quiet during the show.» What is a concert? | A tall building in a busy town | *A show where people play music or sing for an audience | A game played on grass | A long walk in the hills
exercise: Lily says «in concert» means singing alone in the bath. What does «in concert» really mean? | Singing alone | *Working together | Shouting at a match | Sitting very still
exercise: «At a concert, play or assembly you stay quiet during the show and clap at the end.» Find and copy the word that means a show with people watching. | end | clap | *concert | play
test: A concert ticket costs £8. How much do 3 tickets cost? | £83 | £5 | *£24 | £11
test: What should you do with your adult in a crowd at a concert? | *Stay close to your adult | Hide under a seat | Run to the front alone | Wander off to find a friend
exam: «Before a concert the orchestra tunes to one note, so everyone plays in tune together.» Why do the players tune before the concert? | So the audience can leave early | So the tickets cost less | *So everyone plays in tune together | So the music stops
